# AppLocker fingerprint tier. Its own PAM service so a finger touch is checked
# by pam_fprintd alone — never answered by a password, and a missing/broken
# fprintd can only fail this stack, never weaken `sudo`.
#
# timeout=6, not longer: a broken reader (libfprint driver errors — seen on a
# Chipsailing CS9711) must not stall the unlock. APPLOCKER_FP=0 turns the whole
# tier off; see README.
#
# Needs libpam-fprintd + an enrolled finger (`fprintd-enroll`). The daemon only
# offers the fingerprint button when `fprintd-list $USER` shows one.
auth       required   pam_fprintd.so   timeout=6
account    required   pam_permit.so
